        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{6x}{(3x^2+2)^2}\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{1}{3x^2+2}+C$",
          "worked": "Inner function: $f(x)=3x^2+2$, so $f'(x)=6x$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int\\frac{6x}{(3x^2+2)^2}\\,dx&=\\int 6x(3x^2+2)^{-2}\\,dx\\\\&=\\frac{(3x^2+2)^{-1}}{-1}+C\\\\&=-\\frac{1}{3x^2+2}+C\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
