        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{9-2x^3}+C$",
          "worked": "Inner function: $f(x)=9-2x^3$, so $f'(x)=-6x^2$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int-\\frac{6x^2}{\\sqrt{9-2x^3}}\\,dx&=\\int-6x^2(9-2x^3)^{-\\frac12}\\,dx\\\\&=\\frac{(9-2x^3)^{\\frac12}}{\\frac12}+C\\\\&=2\\sqrt{9-2x^3}+C\\end{aligned}$$",
